1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,690
Hello everyone, I am Raiyan Rahman and
this is Unsick.

2
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:07,230
Bangladeshi farmer often sprays more
pesticides than their crop need.

3
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:09,530
Usually on a dealer's word,

4
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:15,290
Kom Bish, meaning less poison, helps them
decide whether to spray at all.

5
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,200
It's a free web app in Bangla.

6
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,460
The farmer agrees to a short consent.

7
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,580
We store no photos or names.

8
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,580
Then they take a close-up photo of one
rice leaf.

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:31,080
[App] Kom Bish is a computer program, not
a government officer.

10
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:33,860
After ticking here, the farmer can upload
their pictures.

11
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:38,980
Here the AI sees bacterial blight,

12
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:43,700
before giving any advice, it asks the
farmer to confirm one symptom.

13
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:47,440
The farmer says yes, the answer spoken in
Bangla,

14
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:50,700
insecticide won't help, so don't buy it.

15
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:54,340
Stop urea and add potash,

16
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,530
that's one spray avoided.

17
00:00:56,550 --> 00:01:00,130
[App] It looks like bacterial leaf blight.

18
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:03,630
[App] Insecticide does not cure it, so
don't buy any.

19
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:05,230
So yeah,

20
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:08,480
here it is asking for confirmation.

21
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,030
[App] It looks like blast.

22
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:13,880
[App] This disease does need a spray, but
done correctly.

23
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,130
[App] Before spraying, read the label on
the packet or bottle

24
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:18,380
[App] and check the colour band.

25
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,980
[App] I can't be sure from this photo.

26
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,900
[App] Better not to answer than to give
wrong advice.

27
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:27,080
So we tested it on photos,

28
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:28,980
of Bangladesh, India and Philippines.

29
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,120
But still the data set is not enough for
it to judge every kind.

30
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:39,350
So our next step would be to train it on a
bigger data set where it can be polished

31
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:41,570
more and can be more accurate.

32
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:46,230
But if we give images from like a real
field, it might give some wrong answers.

33
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:52,330
So the only thing we can do is train it on
local field photos and

34
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:57,930
as well as inputs. So yes, this is the
prototype for Kom Bish, thank you.
